YW5k\0AIE5ldHdvcmtzIEluVlBOIFNlcnZlcjCCASIwDQYJKoZIhvcNAQEBBQADggEPADCC\0AAQoCggEBAMBDlCxv4cvmueytzFCk13iPqhzR0AZDK4s0Zo37RqHMiqDF0UdpRBGE\0A0VyK/WWi4JMAiTatfmZXUAAudma8JAphbt9KVpoUFE7CF0eWyYebmWUKlvgs/DT6\0AtMHeavYIbwTQqMTlVUp/n8g8J70muduGut5zsGDSFq+IwvJAWSMvyvLmopkXQslT\0Aj7pWEd1EH6MjGg8V84VzTYtL+XSbwAWALx/LZZYyp5S7LxLLBFycmTaQfLb1clDC\0AOA5HadMeEK2h4kRRNwz/wqLBOaO1H28s/BE9Y7QAKyzcDrRYqTKQRZ8TbQsqwhK4\0A7gLULMXGJCOKRI3X+ZKdNoWZoHchIVECAwEAAaNTMFEwHQYDVR0OBBYEFJQ2DCb6\0A2KVmHiKAz277Z+fiLuQlMB8GA1UdIwQYMBaAFJQ2DCb62KVmHiKAz277Z+fiLuQl\0AMA8GA1UdEwEB/wQFMAMBAf8wDQYJKoZIhvcNAQELBQADggEBAGX+CRKYLfqu2CWt\0AxraFavASySI+1uFuIJWjR5XION5BLqmW2Ki+Y+4UjpGUmnEYtThM8PmiL0gHzW19\0AjR5OTuK7d9jydvr44/lihFV1ntEUTecokFQmx7dozUW26eFG2297kQCN22FPd35c\0AO8odsY89owuQohvaf9l+4axNaQfSPTsTxkGT4BHNbICUfvaoJ0sw8ooXvs4rNVLY\0ABSnmL3a1Mw6SpyTPVJt+N4PlvhxeIGAWU0jxJ7zGG83XmfEKqJwZQdndSg9BqCQ6\0Al0dczYZWImPJj7hvHV/PIMj36lur1bXnqZgQ5tV2UwlDcwfHyzFKmuzWNZ8qTl2d\0AcrmYF94=\0A-----END CERTIFICATE-----\0A\0A</ca>\0A\0A# Verify server certificate by checking\0A# that the certicate has the nsCertType\0A# field set to "server".  This is an\0A# important precaution to protect against\0A# a potential attack discussed here:\0A#  http://openvpn.net/howto.html#mitm\0A#\0A# To use this feature, you will need to generate\0A# your server certificates with the nsCertType\0A# field set to "server".  The build-key-server\0A# script in the easy-rsa folder will do this.\0A;ns-cert-type server\0A\0A; auth-user-pass auth.txt\0A\0A# If a tls-auth key is used on the server\0A# then every client must also have the key.\0A;tls-auth ta.key 1\0A\0A# Select a cryptographic cipher.\0A# If the cipher option is used on the server\0A# then you must also specify it here.\0Acipher AES-256-CBC\0A\0A# Enable compression on the VPN link.\0A# Don't enable this unless it is also\0A# enabled in the server config file.\0Acomp-lzo\0A\0A\0Apush-peer-info\0A\0Aignore-unknown-option compress comp-lzo\0A\0A# Set log file verbosity.\0Averb 3\0A